{title: 006 - O Worship the Lord}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #006 • SOUTHAMPTON • 13.10.13.10}
{lyricist: J. S. B. Monsell}
{composer: Edwin Barnes}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 6}
{meta: tune SOUTHAMPTON}
{meta: meter 13.10.13.10}
{meta: category Worship - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]O worship [F]the [C]Lord in the beauty of holiness,
[C]Bow down before Him, [Am]His glory [D7]proclaim;
[C]With gold of obedience, and incense [G]of lowliness,
[C/G]Kneel and adore [Am]Him; [C/G]the Lord is [G7]His [C]name.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Low at His [F]feet [C]lay thy burden [G]of [C]carefulness,
[C]High on His heart He [Am]will bear it [D7]for [G]thee,
[C]Comfort thy sorrows, and [F/C]answer [G]thy prayerfulness,
[C/G]Guiding thy [Am]steps as [C/G]may best for [G7]thee [C]be.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Fear not to enter His courts [G]in [C]the slenderness
[C]Of the poor wealth thou [Am]wouldst reckon [D7]as [G]thine;
[C]Truth in its beauty, and [F/C]love [C]in [G]its tenderness,
[C/G]These are the offerings to lay [G7]on His [C]shrine.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]These, though we bring them in trembling and fearfulness,
[C]He will accept for [Am]the name that [D7]is [G]dear;
[C]Mornings of joy give for evenings [G]of tearfulness,
[C/G]Trust for our [Am]trembling, [C/G]and hope for [G7]our [C]fear.
{end_of_verse}
